<title>POLAND: USDA GUARANTEES $11 MLN IN KREDYT LOANS.</title>
<headline>USDA GUARANTEES $11 MLN IN KREDYT LOANS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture has guaranteed $11 million in loans from Polish bank Kredyt Bank SA for farm imports from the United States, the bank said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The statement said the USDA would guarantee up to $25 million in short-term loans in Poland and up to $5 million in long-term loans.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
